      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing half of the Mo fraction with V produces NbZrTiHfMo0.5V0.5.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy can be prepared by arc melting followed by homogenization at approximately 1200°C and natural cooling.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial replacement of Mo by V reduces the overall electronegativity difference in NbZrTiHfMo0.5V0.5.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing the electronegativity difference alleviates local bonding heterogeneity.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive electronegativity mismatch and local bonding heterogeneity hinder dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Introducing V promotes dislocation mobility and consequently increases compressive plastic deformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "NbZrTiHfMo0.5V0.5 will remain a single-phase disordered BCC alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The V-containing alloy will retain sufficient lattice distortion to maintain high strength.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lattice distortion contributes to the strength of the alloy.",
